*.token
.env
.mcpregistry_*
.token-cache.json
node_modules/

# [2026-08-06] EDITOR/BACKUP POLLUTION — MIRRORS .npmignore.
# These patterns existed in .npmignore since the v0.9.3 hotfix and were NEVER
# added here, so the two ignore files protected two different surfaces and only
# one of them was covered. A `git add -A` today staged 23 untracked files —
# five license/server backups, seven _backups/ snapshots, hero.png and six
# internal marketing drafts — for a commit to a PUBLIC GitHub repo.
# .npmignore gets no vote on what git publishes, and GitHub is the more
# browsable of the two surfaces: a reader needs no install to see it.
*.bak
*.bak.*
*.pre-*
*.orig
*.swp
*.tmp
_backups/
.stale-drafts-backup-*/

# Internal drafts — already excluded from the npm tarball by name in .npmignore.
# Same decision, applied to the other publishing surface.
HACKERNEWS-POST.md
HN-PINNED-COMMENT.md
MCPMARKET-LISTING.md
PRODUCT-HUNT-LISTING.md
SMITHERY_DESCRIPTION.md
SMITHERY_VERIFICATION_REQUEST.md
guesty-partnership-email.md
tripadvisor-partnership-email.md
hero.png
